{"name":"Greenbriar","hex":"#245d3f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"greenbriar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of greenbrier."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greenbriar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Smilax","blocks":[{"text":"Smilax is a genus of about 300–350 species, found in the tropics and subtropics worldwide. They are climbing flowering plants, many of which are woody and/or thorny, in the monocotyledon family Smilacaceae, native throughout the tropical and subtropical regions of the world. \nCommon names include catbriers, greenbriers, prickly-ivys and smilaxes. Sarsaparilla is a name used specifically for the Neotropical S. ornata as well as a catch-all term in particular for American species. Occasionally, the non-woody species such as the smooth herbaceous greenbrier are separated as genus Nemexia; they are commonly known by the rather ambiguous name carrion flowers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Smilax_aspera.jpg/330px-Smilax_aspera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smilax","wikidata":"Q165315"},{"title":"Greenwood/Greenbriar","blocks":[{"text":"Greenwood/Greenbriar is a residential neighbourhood in the northwest quadrant of Calgary, Alberta. It is bounded by the Trans-Canada Highway to the south, the Bow River to the north, Stoney Trail to the west and the community of Bowness to the east. Canada Olympic Park borders the neighbourhood to the south. The community consists primarily of a mobile home park, Greenwood Village; maps since the early 1980s have shown proposed streets south of the mobile home park and north of the Trans-Canada Highway, but as of 2019 development had begun on a community named Greenwich that would primarily include semi-detached homes, commercial businesses & restaurants."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwood%2FGreenbriar","wikidata":"Q14252577"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Smilax_sp._climber.jpg/500px-Smilax_sp._climber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Smilax_sp._climber.jpg/1280px-Smilax_sp._climber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Smilax_sp._climber.jpg/500px-Smilax_sp._climber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Smilax sp. climber at Howrah district, West Bengal, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmilax_sp._climber.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Kaniska_canace_on_Smilax_china_07i1804.jpg/500px-Kaniska_canace_on_Smilax_china_07i1804.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Kaniska_canace_on_Smilax_china_07i1804.jpg/500px-Kaniska_canace_on_Smilax_china_07i1804.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blue admiral (Kaniska canace) caterpillar on China smilax (S. china)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKaniska_canace_on_Smilax_china_07i1804.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Diosgenin_planar.png/500px-Diosgenin_planar.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Diosgenin_planar.png/1280px-Diosgenin_planar.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Diosgenin_planar.png/500px-Diosgenin_planar.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diosgenin is found in S. menispermoidea.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%